{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787156150,"nonce":"4yF5/sDq6uzktIvLmtt71HF8swQ=","message":"**Owner ruling, 2026-08-19: `generation` dies with `alert_groups`. Which closes the question comment #2 raised, and demotes this ticket from a design decision to a cleanup.**\n\n⛔ **Comments #1 and #2 are both superseded. Do not pick from either.** #1 offered four rollover axes; #2 argued the real question was whether `refire_grace` survives the one-Case ruling. Both assumed `refire_grace` still decides something. It does not.\n\n**`refire_grace` has no consumer.** Every live reference is settings plumbing:\n\n```\n identity/domain/settings.go:39    KeyRefireGrace = \"refire_grace_s\"\n                          :132     MinRefireGraceSeconds = 600\n                          :169     bounds {Min: 600, Max: 86400}\n identity/domain/org.go:108,200,244,266   field, default, seed, fallback\n identity/api/{dto,mapper,settings}.go    wire, patch, read-back\n identity/repository/orgs.go:40,68,84     stored blob\n platform/tuning/defaults.go:82           DefaultRefireGrace = 1200s\n ingestion/domain/bounds.go:126           a COMMENT deriving a bound from MinRefireGrace\n ── and nothing else. ZERO reads in alerts/ grouping/ notification/ ingestion/ app/.\n```\n\n`routingCommand` (`alerts/service/lifecycle.go:867-880`) is where it used to be consumed. It now passes **`ResolveGrace`**, not `RefireGrace`, while its own doc comment still reads *\"the two clock readings and the re-fire grace that resolves T7 against T8\"* — and T8 was retired by ADR 0040 (`alerts/domain/lifecycle.go:114-118`: *\"T8, which used to reopen the same one inside refire_grace, is retired and a closed Case is now strictly terminal\"*). The mechanism went; the setting stayed.\n\n⭐ **And `platform/tuning/defaults.go:75-82` already said so, before anyone noticed:**\n\n\u003e *\"every re-fire opened a new episode, a new generation and a new Slack root card, **with a setting on the screen that looked like it should have stopped it**.\"*\n\nADR 0026 read that as \"the default is too small\" and raised 600 → 1200s to cover 86.5% of the rule corpus. Then ADR 0040 removed the mechanism the raise was feeding. The tuning derivation is now an argument about the correct value of a number nothing reads.\n\n\n```\n generation           dies with alert_groups\n group_close_delay_s  its only job is closing generations\n                      (consumed at app/adapters.go:734 → LifecyclePolicy{CloseDelay})\n                      → dies with them\n refire_grace_s       already decides nothing\n thread length        MaxThreadReplies = 30 / NeedsFreshRoot / dispatch.go:770\n                      — Case-independent, stays, stays nested\n conversation ends    the Case ends; channel_threads binds to the Case\n```\n\nA card per re-fire is **already today's behaviour** — same tuning comment. So the drop changes no observable Slack behaviour, which is the strongest argument that no rollover rule is owed: the thing a rollover rule would have to preserve was never working.\n\n\n`refire_grace_s` is on the settings screen, bounds-validated (600–86400), defaulted from a corpus derivation, patchable and stored — and no code path reads it. That is the `tools/lintreach` defect class (\"declarations wired to nothing\"), except lintreach walks Go declarations and cannot see a live setting whose only reader is its own CRUD. `group_close_delay_s` becomes the same thing the moment `alert_groups` goes.\n\nBoth should leave the settings surface with `alert_groups`, the same shape as the reminder's four keys going with the reminder (`bd0fb1d`) rather than being retired — the owner's standing ruling is delete, do not retire, because ghost references at launch are the cost.\n\n⚠️ **One thing to check before deleting, not after.** `ingestion/domain/bounds.go:126-128` derives an ingestion bound with reference to `MinRefireGrace` — *\"`MinRefireGrace` in `identity/domain` is `2 × DedupTTL`, so every legal … OBSERVABLE and INSIDE the grace\"* — and names a test, `TestTheReplayWindowIsStrictlyInsideRefireGrace`. That is a comment and a test, not a runtime read, but the replay-window bound may be pinned to a constant that is about to disappear. Establish what that test actually asserts before removing `MinRefireGraceSeconds`, or a bound loses its stated derivation silently.\n\n⚠️ **Also worth fixing while in there:** the `refire_grace` ⇄ `group_close_delay` \"pinning\" is two independent literals in `platform/tuning/defaults.go` (`:82` and the `DefaultGroupCloseDelay` below it), both `1200 * time.Second`, with a comment insisting *\"the equality is the whole point rather than a coincidence\"*. Nothing enforces it — the `4aea61e` shape. Moot if both are deleted; a live trap if only one is.\n\n**Retitle candidate:** this ticket is now *\"`refire_grace_s` and `group_close_delay_s` are org-facing settings that decide nothing, and they leave with `alert_groups`\"*. Left as-is for the owner to rename, since the current title states a rollover gap that the answer above says is not a gap.","files":null}]}